Done. Added `store::rename` to `rust/src/store.rs:40`.

**What it does:**
- Scans `dir` for the file whose stored content has `old_id` as its first field (the same identification `load_all` uses), preserving body and pinned state.
- Writes the note under `new_id` with `new_title`, keeping the same `SEP`-delimited format (`id SEP title SEP pinned SEP body`).
- Removes the old file so nothing remains under the old id.
- Returns a `NotFound` error if no stored note matches `old_id`.

**Verified:**
- `cargo build` clean; `cargo test` (existing `tests/basic.rs`) still passes.
- Temporary test (removed afterward) confirmed: after `rename`, `load_all` returns exactly one note with the new id/title, body and `#tags` preserved, `pinned` preserved, and `old.note` no longer on disk.

One design note: matching is by the note's stored id (first content field), not just the filename, so a note whose filename doesn't match its internal id still renames correctly.


